│ patch_name               │ stratified_lookahead_sampling                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent random placement samples with deterministic stratified samples over   │
│                          │ the empty-cell rank range.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current lookahead draws samples with replacement, so the same hypothetical placement  │
│                          │ can be evaluated multiple times while other regions are missed. This substantially        │
│                          │ increases variance, especially with only 18 and 7 samples. Moreover, each candidate       │
│                          │ direction receives different random samples, making direction comparisons noisy.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Stratified sampling divides all currently empty-cell ranks into equal-sized intervals and │
│                          │ takes one deterministic pseudo-random rank from each interval. This guarantees broad      │
│                          │ coverage without duplicates, remains representative of the uniform placement process, and │
│                          │ uses common random ranks for comparable lookahead states. It should make decisions more   │
│                          │ stable and improve expected final clustering without increasing search cost.              │
