│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ stratified_boundary_shaping                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent random placement samples with stratified samples over the empty-cell  │
│                          │ rank space. The current Monte Carlo sampling can select the same empty cell multiple      │
│                          │ times and leave large portions of the board unrepresented, making direction selection     │
│                          │ noisy. Stratification preserves broad coverage at both lookahead levels while retaining a │
│                          │ randomized offset.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also add a penalty for adjacent candies of different flavors. Near a full board,          │
│                          │ minimizing mixed-color edges is a useful proxy for obtaining compact flavor regions and   │
│                          │ complements the component-square objective: component score rewards already completed     │
│                          │ merges, while this term helps select moves that create cleaner interfaces before those    │
│                          │ merges occur. Its coefficient grows with the turn because mixed adjacency is much more    │
│                          │ meaningful as empty space disappears.                                                     │
