│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetric_stratified_lookahead                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Exploit the rotational symmetry of the board by evaluating both vertical flavor strips    │
│                          │ and their 90-degree-rotated horizontal equivalent. The original region heuristic          │
│                          │ artificially commits all flavors to columns, even though horizontal clustering is equally │
│                          │ valid and may be substantially easier given the current arrangement. Using the better of  │
│                          │ the two layouts preserves the intended separation pressure while allowing the search to   │
│                          │ discover either orientation.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also replace independently sampled placement indices with stratified samples. The old     │
│                          │ Monte Carlo sampling can select the same empty cell multiple times, wasting expensive     │
│                          │ lookahead evaluations and increasing decision noise. One random sample from each          │
│                          │ equal-sized index interval covers the full empty-cell order more evenly while retaining   │
│                          │ randomness.                                                                               │
