│ patch_name               │ unique_lookahead_samples                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The lookahead currently samples future empty-cell ranks with replacement. This wastes a   │
│                          │ nontrivial fraction of the fixed simulation budget by evaluating identical placements     │
│                          │ multiple times, especially when the number of empty cells becomes moderate. Sample future │
│                          │ placements uniformly without replacement using a partial Fisher-Yates shuffle instead.    │
│                          │ This preserves an unbiased estimate over empty cells while increasing effective board     │
│                          │ coverage and reducing decision variance, with negligible overhead relative to copying,    │
│                          │ tilting, and evaluating game states.                                                      │
