│ patch_description        │ Use common deterministic stratified rollout placements for all candidate directions at    │
│                          │ the same turn/depth. The current random phase is independently consumed while evaluating  │
│                          │ different root actions, introducing Monte-Carlo noise directly into the direction         │
│                          │ comparison. A phase derived only from the simulated turn and depth makes every competing  │
│                          │ action estimate its expectation using the same empty-cell ranks, while still varying the  │
│                          │ sampled ranks over time. This should make greedy action selection more stable without     │
│                          │ increasing computational cost.                                                            │
