│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the stronger current-program idea of sampling distinct empty-cell    │
│                          │ insertion ranks, while replacing the costly `vector<Candy>` state representation and      │
│                          │ repeated candy-list rebuilding with a compact fixed 100-cell board.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new implementation:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses a flat fixed-size board, making state copies cheap during lookahead.               │
│                          │ - Performs tilts without rebuilding auxiliary vectors.                                    │
│                          │ - Computes all evaluation terms directly from the board in one or two scans.              │
│                          │ - Retains the original target-strip, component-connectivity, center-of-mass, and edge     │
│                          │ heuristics.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Uses distinct sampled placement ranks as in the higher-scoring current program.         │
│                          │ - Increases lookahead sampling to `{22, 9}` because the fixed-board implementation        │
│                          │ substantially reduces search overhead.                                                    │
