│ patch_name               │ particle_mpc                                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces shallow sampled expectimax with a particle-based model-predictive           │
│                          │ controller. For every possible current tilt, it runs multiple common-random-number future │
│                          │ simulations. Each simulation inserts several upcoming known flavors at random legal       │
│                          │ cells, then uses a fast greedy rollout policy to choose future tilts. The current         │
│                          │ direction is selected by the average terminal quality across particles.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The board representation is compact and avoids rebuilding candy vectors. Evaluation       │
│                          │ combines exact same-flavor component-square value, adjacency, flavor compactness, and a   │
│                          │ fading strip-separation prior. The auxiliary terms disappear toward the end, so late      │
│                          │ decisions increasingly optimize the official connectivity objective directly.             │
