│ patch_name               │ fast_montecarlo                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the higher-scoring randomized Monte-Carlo placement sampling from    │
│                          │ the current program while replacing the expensive `vector<Candy>` state representation    │
│                          │ and repeated candy-list rebuilding with a compact fixed-size board state.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation uses:                                                                  │
│                          │ - A 100-cell `uint8_t` board and explicit occupied count, making state copies during      │
│                          │ lookahead much cheaper.                                                                   │
│                          │ - Fused board scans for center-of-mass, region, and edge heuristics.                      │
│                          │ - Integer-index BFS for connected-component scoring.                                      │
│                          │ - A slightly expanded lookahead sampling budget (`{20, 8}`), enabled by the substantially │
│                          │ cheaper state copies and tilt operations.                                                 │
│                          │ - A special late-game shortcut when only one empty cell remains, avoiding redundant       │
│                          │ direction branches.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It preserves the required interactive input/output protocol and keeps the required evolve │
│                          │ markers.                                                                                  │
