│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ common_rank_sampling                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace per-node stratified random phases with partial Fisher–Yates samples drawn once    │
│                          │ per decision and shared by all four root actions.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The earlier no-replacement approach outperformed deterministic stratification, likely     │
│                          │ because it retains broader random coverage without repeatedly evaluating the same         │
│                          │ insertion rank. The current policy also draws a separate random phase inside each root    │
│                          │ action and descendant state, adding avoidable comparison noise: directions are judged     │
│                          │ against different chance outcomes. This edit creates one distinct-rank schedule for the   │
│                          │ first forecasted placement and one for the second forecasted placement, then reuses them  │
│                          │ for every corresponding chance node in the current action decision. The schedules remain  │
│                          │ fresh between real turns, retain no-replacement coverage, and make root-direction         │
│                          │ comparisons substantially fairer.                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
