│ patch_description        │ Add a targeted second Monte-Carlo batch for ambiguous root decisions. The existing search │
│                          │ already uses distinct chance ranks, which is good for coverage, but each root direction   │
│                          │ currently receives an independent sample set, so close root values can be selected due to │
│                          │ sampling noise.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ First evaluate all four directions with the established `{18,7}` budget. If the best and  │
│                          │ second-best directions are sufficiently close, independently re-evaluate only those two   │
│                          │ with a smaller `{8,3}` batch and combine the estimates weighted by their first-chance     │
│                          │ sample counts. This preserves full search quality for clear decisions while spending      │
│                          │ modest additional computation only where it can change the selected action. The           │
│                          │ worst-case added leaf work is small relative to the baseline and is avoided entirely on   │
│                          │ unambiguous turns.                                                                        │
